  "source_text": "Title: Classic Cheeseburger on Brioche\nServings: 4\n\nIngredients (component | amount unit | name | prep_style | pantry food_id):\n- Beef Patty | 400 g | beef ground beef |  | 000011\n- Beef Patty | 0.5 tsp | Garlic Powder |  | 000643\n- Beef Patty | 0.5 tsp | Ground Onion |  | 000644\n- Beef Patty | 5 g | kosher salt |  | 000293\n- Beef Patty | 0.5 tsp | ground black pepper |  | 000285\n- Burger Assembly | 150 g | brioche |  | 000336\n- Burger Assembly | 40 g | cheddar |  | 000193\n- Burger Assembly | 20 g | lettuce |  | 000079\n- Burger Assembly | 60 g | Roma tomatoes, chopped |  | IMP-6d4cd7\n- Burger Assembly | 20 g | pickled cucumbers (dill pickles) |  | 000446\n- Burger Assembly | 15 g | unsalted butter |  | 000212\n\nSteps in order (component | phase | minutes | text):\n1. Beef Patty | Prep |  | Divide the chilled ground beef into two equal 200g portions.\n2. Burger Assembly | Prep |  | Slice the brioche buns horizontally and slice the Roma tomatoes into thin uniform rounds.\n3. Beef Patty | Prep |  | Form each portion into a patty about 10cm in diameter, slightly wider than your brioche bun.\n4. Burger Assembly | Prep |  | Rinse the lettuce leaves under cold water and pat them completely dry using a kitchen towel.\n5. Beef Patty | Prep |  | Press a small dimple into the center of each patty with your thumb to prevent shrinking and bulging during cooking.\n6. Burger Assembly | Cook |  | Spread softened butter onto the cut sides of the brioche bun halves.\n7. Beef Patty | Prep |  | In a small bowl, whisk together the garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and black pepper.\n8. Burger Assembly | Cook |  | Place the buns in a separate skillet over medium heat and toast for 1-2 minutes until golden and crisp.\n9. Beef Patty | Prep |  | Season the exterior of both patties generously on both sides with the spice mixture.\n10. Burger Assembly | Cook |  | During the final minute of cooking the patties, place cheddar slices on top and cover the pan to melt the cheese.\n11. Beef Patty | Cook |  | Heat a cast-iron skillet over high heat. SAFETY: Wash your hands and all surfaces that contacted raw meat thoroughly with soap.\n12. Burger Assembly | Serve |  | Lay the bottom toasted bun on a plate and place a piece of lettuce followed by the tomato slices.\n13. Beef Patty | Cook |  | Place patties in the hot pan and sear for 4 minutes until a dark brown crust forms, then flip.\n14. Burger Assembly | Serve |  | Carefully place the cheesed beef patty onto the tomatoes and top with the pickled cucumber slices.\n15. Beef Patty | Serve |  | Remove the patties from the heat and let them rest for 2 minutes to allow the juices to redistribute.\n16. Burger Assembly | Serve |  | Finish by placing the top bun over the pickles and serve immediately while hot.",
